{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And you shall not swear by My name.</b> Why is it stated? Since it is stated ״לֹא תִשָּׂא אֶת שֵׁם ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ לַשָּׁוְא״ (Exodus 20), one might think he is liable only for the special Name — from where to include all the epithets? Scripture says: ״וְלֹא תִשָּׁבְעוּ בִשְׁמִי לַשָּׁקֶר״ — every name that I have (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:07.268044458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}